{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK6YBvQWGmWUkG7FLJMb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`HttpResponse(memoryview(b\"My Content\")).content` now returns `b'My Content'` instead of `b'<memory at 0x...>'`. The `httpwrappers` and `responses` test suites pass.\n\nThe fix is two small changes in `django/http/response.py`:\n- **`make_bytes`**: a `memoryview` is now turned into bytes directly, the same way `bytes` already was. Before, it fell through to the generic `str(value)` path, which produced the `<memory at ...>` text.\n- **`content` setter**: a `memoryview` is now treated as a single value, like `bytes` and `str`. Without this, the setter would have seen it as a list of separate chunks because a `memoryview` can be looped over.\n\n`StreamingHttpResponse` now also accepts `memoryview` chunks, which I checked with `[memoryview(b'ab')]`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":19109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":681},"output_tokens":288,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b0ce36e-585b-490f-b2ea-804fafda62a2","uuid":"11d5bc7e-e5fb-4b36-b8f8-27ed07ba8ab0","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:47:42.926Z","request_id":"req_011ChK6YBmE2kwSoMsj8Z7LH"}
